@startuml
' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Mencius Rule-2 / Rule-3 paper bug — canonical Lamport / sequence
' diagram for the scenario in bug.md.
'
' Render: plantuml bug.puml  → bug.png
'         plantuml -tsvg bug.puml → bug.svg
'
' Companion artifact: bug.svg (hand-built, publication-quality).
' Source spec:        Mencius_bugged.spur
' Narrative:          bug.md
' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

title **Mencius Protocol 𝒫 — Rule-2 / Rule-3 safety bug**\n//Canonical 3-server, no-crash scenario from bug.md//

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 4
skinparam noteFontSize 11
skinparam noteFontName "DejaVu Sans Mono"
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam participantPadding 18
skinparam BoxPadding 12

participant "**client**"      as cl
participant "**p0**\nowns {0,3,…}"   as p0
participant "**p1**\nowns {1,4,…}\n//revoker//"   as p1
participant "**p2**\nowns {2,5,…}\n//proposer//"  as p2

' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Starting-state header (identical across nodes after Init(me, peers))
' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
note across #E8F0FE
**Starting state** (post-`Init`, Mencius_bugged.spur:144–157)
====
For every node pᵢ ∈ {p0, p1, p2}, n = 3:
| variable             | value                                          |
| ``self``             | ``i``                                          |
| ``my_index``         | ``i``  (next slot it owns; owner(j) = j % 3)  |
| ``expected``         | ``0``                                          |
| ``est_index``        | ``{0:0, 1:1, 2:2}``                            |
| ``prepared_ballot``, ``has_prepared``       | ``{}`` (implicit ``(0, owner(j))``) |
| ``accepted_ballot``, ``has_accepted``, ``accepted_value`` | ``{}`` |
| ``learned_flags``, ``learned_value``        | ``{}``               |
| ``revoke_*``                                | ``{}``               |
| ``kv_store``, ``applied_cmds``, ``pending_requests`` | ``{}``      |
| ``next_req_id``      | ``i`` (strides by n)                           |
| ``links``            | ``{0:fifo(p0), 1:fifo(p1), 2:fifo(p2)}``       |
| ``need_to_skip``, ``skip_timer_active``     | ``{}``               |
----
**Legend.** Ballots = ``(round, leader)``.  Owner(slot) = slot mod 3.
Every inter-node message travels over a **per-pair FIFO link** —
ordering is preserved //within// a link but pairs are independent.
Slot 2 messages: **red**.  Slot 5 messages: **blue**.
Revoke messages (ballot ≥ 1): **purple**.  Discarded: dashed with ✗.
end note

' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
== Phase A — Triggers ==

cl -> p2 : **①** ClientWrite("k", uid=//v//)
note right of p2 #FFF3E0
``on_client_request(v)`` (line 525):
``proposed[2] = v``;
``my_index: 2 → 5``;
``persist()``;
``broadcast_propose(2, (0,2), v)``
end note

rnote over p1 #F3E5F5
**②** //"suspect" timer fires//
``on_suspect(2)`` → ``start_revoke(2)``
ballot = ``(1, p1)``
``broadcast_prepare(2, (1,1))``
end rnote

' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
== Phase B — Two broadcasts race on independent FIFO links ==

p2 -[#C62828]> p0 : **③** PROPOSE(2, (0,2), v)
p2 -[#C62828]> p1 : **④** PROPOSE(2, (0,2), v)
p2 -[#C62828]> p2 : **⑤** PROPOSE(2, (0,2), v)

p1 -[#6A1B9A]> p0 : **⑥** PREPARE(2, (1,1))
p1 -[#6A1B9A]> p1 : **⑦** PREPARE(2, (1,1))
p1 -[#6A1B9A]> p2 : **⑧** PREPARE(2, (1,1))

' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
== Phase C — Handler effects (per-pair link ordering breaks symmetrically) ==

note over p0 #E8F5E9
At **p0**, on link ``p2 → p0`` event ③ is delivered //before// ⑥.
``HandlePropose(2, (0,2), v)`` (line 596):
guard passes, owner ≠ self → ``on_suggestion(2)`` (line 435):
  ``fill_q_skips(2, 2)``: ``est_index[2] = 5``
  skip p0's own ``[my_index=0, 2)``:
    ``learn_slot(0, nil)``;  ``my_index: 0 → 3``
  ``defer_skips(q=2, [0])``: ``need_to_skip[1] = [0]``
then accept: ``accepted[2] = (0,2)/v``, ``has_accepted[2]=true``.
end note
p0 -[#C62828]> p2 : **⑨** ACCEPT(2, (0,2), v)

note over p0 #E8F5E9
Then ⑥ arrives at p0:
``HandlePrepare(2, (1,1))`` (line 686): ballot > prep=(0,2) →
``prepared_ballot[2] = (1,1)``.
end note
p0 -[#6A1B9A]> p1 : **⑩** ACK(2, (1,1), //has_accepted=true, acc=(0,2)/v//)

rnote over p1 #FFEBEE
At **p1**, the self-link delivers ⑦ first:
``HandlePrepare(2, (1,1))`` → ``prepared_ballot[2] = (1,1)``.
end rnote
p1 -[#6A1B9A]> p1 : **⑪** ACK(2, (1,1), //has_accepted=false//)

rnote over p1 #FFEBEE
Then ④ arrives at p1:
``HandlePropose(2, (0,2), v)`` (line 614):
``ballot_gte((0,2), (1,1))`` is **false** → **✗ REJECTED**
//no ACCEPT sent — this is the load-bearing rejection.//
end rnote

note over p2 #E8F5E9
At **p2**, self-link delivers ⑤ first:
``HandlePropose(2, (0,2), v)``: owner == self, accept directly:
``accepted[2] = (0,2)/v``.
end note
p2 -[#C62828]> p2 : **⑫** ACCEPT(2, (0,2), v)

note over p2 #E8F5E9
Then ⑧ arrives at p2:
``HandlePrepare(2, (1,1))`` → ``prepared_ballot[2] = (1,1)``,
includes prior accept in ACK.
end note
p2 -[#6A1B9A]> p1 : **⑬** ACK(2, (1,1), //has_accepted=true, acc=(0,2)/v//)

' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
== Phase D — Ballot-0 quorum at {p0, p2} chooses //v// ==

note over p2 #E8F5E9
``HandleAccept`` tallies for slot 2 at ballot (0,2):
self ⑫ + p0 ⑨ → count = 2 ≥ majority.
``learn_slot(2, v)``;  ``broadcast_learn(2, v)``.
end note

p2 -[#C62828]> p0 : **⑭** LEARN(2, v)
p2 -[#C62828]> p1 : **⑮** LEARN(2, v)
p2 -[#C62828]> p2 : **⑯** LEARN(2, v)

' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
== Phase E — Second client write (the trigger) ==

cl -> p2 : **⑰** ClientWrite("k", uid=//v'//)
note right of p2 #FFF3E0
``on_client_request(v')``:
``proposed[5] = v'``;  ``my_index: 5 → 8``;
``broadcast_propose(5, (0,2), v')``
end note

p2 -[#1565C0]> p0 : **⑱** PROPOSE(5, (0,2), v')
p2 -[#1565C0]> p1 : **⑲** PROPOSE(5, (0,2), v')
p2 -[#1565C0]> p2 : **⑳** PROPOSE(5, (0,2), v')

' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
== Phase F — The bug fires on p1 ==

rnote over p1 #FFCDD2
**⚠ BUG.**  The ``p2 → p1`` FIFO link ordered ⑮ before ⑲.
If ⑲'s ``HandlePropose`` task is dispatched and runs through
``on_suggestion(5)`` before ⑮'s ``HandleLearn`` sets
``learned_flags[2]``, then:

``on_suggestion(5)`` (line 435) at p1:
  ``fill_q_skips(2, 5)`` (line 412):
    j=2, owner(2)=2  →  **``learn_slot(2, nil)``**   ← //BUG//
    j=3 (owner p0, skip), j=4 (owner p1, skip)
  ``est_index[2] = 8``
  skip p1's own ``[my_index=1, 5)``:
    ``learn_slot(1, nil)``, ``learn_slot(4, nil)``;
    ``my_index: 1 → 7``
then accept slot 5: ``accepted[5] = (0,2)/v'``.

**p1's** ``learned_value[2] = ⊥`` (no-op).
**p0/p2's** ``learned_value[2] = v``.
end rnote

p1 -[#1565C0]> p2 : **㉑** ACCEPT(5, (0,2), v')

' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
== Phase G — Masked LEARN and stalled revoke ==

p2 -[#C62828,dashed]->x p1 : **⑮'** LEARN(2, v) //(delivered, but `is_learned(2)` already true → **✗ discarded**, line 679)//

note over p1 #F3E5F5
p1's revoke Phase 1 tallies ACKs ⑪ + ⑩ + ⑬ → majority.
``revoke_best_value[2] = v`` (highest accepted_ballot = (0,2)).
Phase 2: ``broadcast_propose(2, (1,1), v)``.
end note

p1 -[#6A1B9A]> p0 : **㉒** PROPOSE(2, (1,1), v)
p1 -[#6A1B9A]> p1 : **㉓** PROPOSE(2, (1,1), v)
p1 -[#6A1B9A]> p2 : **㉔** PROPOSE(2, (1,1), v)

note over p0, p2 #ECEFF1
At every receiver ``is_learned(2) == true`` →
``HandlePropose`` short-circuits to **``HandleLearn(2, learned_value[2])``**
back to p1 (line 599).
end note

p0 -[#C62828,dashed]->x p1 : **㉕** LEARN(2, v)   //(✗ p1 already has nil)//
p1 -[#C62828,dashed]->x p1 : **㉖** LEARN(2, ⊥)   //(self, no-op)//
p2 -[#C62828,dashed]->x p1 : **㉗** LEARN(2, v)   //(✗ p1 already has nil)//

note over p2 #E8F5E9
Slot 5 quorum: ⑳-self + ㉑ → majority. ``learn_slot(5, v')``.
//Slot 5 commits cleanly on every node — only slot 2 diverges.//
end note

p2 -[#1565C0]> p0 : **㉘** LEARN(5, v')
p2 -[#1565C0]> p1 : **㉙** LEARN(5, v')
p2 -[#1565C0]> p2 : **㉚** LEARN(5, v')

' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
== Phase H — The violation becomes observable ==

note over p0 #FFF3E0
//(Glue:)// once a ClientWrite from p0 fills slot 0
//or// p0's deferred ``need_to_skip[1]=[0]`` flushes to p1 and a
symmetric p1 SUGGEST advances both ``expected`` counters past slot 2,
the divergent values become observable to clients.
end note

cl -> p1 : **㉛** Read("k")
note right of p1 #FFCDD2
p1 applies committed log:
  slot 0 = nil, slot 1 = nil, slot 2 = **nil**, slot 4 = nil, slot 5 = v'
``kv_store["k"] = [u_{v'}]``  //(only v', no v)//
end note
p1 --> cl : returns ``[u_{v'}]``

cl -> p0 : **㉜** Read("k")
note right of p0 #E8F5E9
p0 applies committed log:
  slot 0 = nil, …, slot 2 = **v**, …, slot 5 = v'
``kv_store["k"] = [u_v, u_{v'}]``
end note
p0 --> cl : returns ``[u_v, u_{v'}]``

' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
note across #FFCDD2
**Divergence (linearizability violated).**
| node | ``learned_value[2]`` | ``Read("k")`` |
| p0   | **v**                | ``[u_v, u_{v'}]`` |
| p1   | **⊥** (no-op)        | ``[u_{v'}]`` |
| p2   | **v**                | ``[u_v, u_{v'}]`` |
end note

@enduml
